          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Majorana spin representation
            is essentially a
            %em real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "spin+representation#RealIrreducibleSpinRepresentationInLorentzSignature"} spin representation – Real representations
            %em complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real structure
            (recalled as def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealStructureOnLinearRepresentation"}
            below).
          %p
            Accordingly a
            %em Majorana spinor
            or
            %em Majorana fermion
            is a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor"} spinor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
            corresponding to such a representation under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wigner+classification"} Wigner classification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            except possibly the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutrinos"} neutrinos
            are Majorana fermions (for neutrinos this remains open). The relevance of Majorana representations is that these appear in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetimes"} super-Minkowski spacetimes
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperPoincareOutlook"}
            below.
          %p
            The terminology
            %em Majorana spinor
            originates in and is standard in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            literature, where it usually refers to the explicit expression of the reality condition in terms of chosen basis components. With standard conventions understood (see prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CliffordAlgebraRepresentation"}
            below), then a complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor"} spinor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi ν
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^{2^\nu}
            (with
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ν
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 2 \nu, 2\nu+1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi t
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo †
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi^t C = \psi^\dagger \Gamma_0
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^T
            denotes forming
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpose+matrices"} transpose matrices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo †
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\dagger = \overline{(-)}^T
            denotes forming
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+adjoint"} hermitian adjoint
            and where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+conjugation+matrix"} charge conjugation matrix
            %em Majorana conjugate
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MajoranaConjugation"}
            below) of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            (the left hand side) coincides with the “Dirac conjugate” (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracConjugate"}
            below) of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            (the right hand side). Equivalently this means that (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} Castellani-D’Auria-Fré, (II.7.22)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo =
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi C
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 0
                    %mi T
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi = J(\psi) \coloneqq C \Gamma_0^T \psi^\ast
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(-)
            is the given real structure (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MajoranaConjugationIsRealStructure"}
            below). See prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheMajoranaConditionInComponents"}
            below.
          %p
            In some dimensions there are no complex spin representations with real structure, but there may be those with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+structure"} quaternionic structure
            = succeed "." do
              %em symplectic Majorana spinor
          %h2#definition Definition
          #MajoranaSpinorGeneral.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \colon Spin(s,t) \longrightarrow GL_{\mathbb{C}}(V)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation"} unitary representation
              of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              is called
              %em Majorana
              if it admits a real structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealStructureOnLinearRepresentation"}
              %em symplectic Majorana
              if it admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+structure"} quaternionic structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealStructureOnLinearRepresentation"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \in V
              is called a
              %em Majorana spinor
              if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(\psi) = \psi
          %h2#InComponents In components
          %p
            We work out in detail what def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MajoranaSpinorGeneral"}
            comes down to in components (i.e. in terms of choices of
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+bases"} linear bases
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} Castellani-D’Auria-Fré
          %h3#conventions_and_notation Conventions and Notation
          %p
            In the following we use standard notation for operations on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
            with entries in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            (and of course these matrices may in particular be complex row/column vectors, which may in particular be single complex numbers):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\ast
                – componentwise
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+conjugation"} complex conjugation
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^T
                –
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpose+matrix"} transpose matrix
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo †
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi T
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi T
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\dagger \coloneqq ((-)^\ast)^T = ((-)^T)^\ast
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A B
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+product"} matrix product
                of two matrices
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            We will be discussing three different pairing operations on complex column vectors
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_1, \psi_2 \in \mathbb{C}^\nu
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 1
                        %mo †
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_1^\dagger \psi_2
                – the standard
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+form"} hermitian form
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℂ
                          %mi ν
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^\nu
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≔
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 1
                        %mo †
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \psi_1,\psi_2\rangle \coloneqq \overline{\psi}_1 \psi_2 \coloneqq \psi_1^\dagger \Gamma_0 \psi_2
                – the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dirac pairing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+form"} hermitian form
                with respect to which the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
                below is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation"} unitary representation
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 1
                        %mi T
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\psi_1,\psi_2) \coloneqq \psi_1^T C \psi_2
                – the
                %em Majorana pairing
                (for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                the
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+conjugation+matrix"} charge conjugation matrix
                %em if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_1
                is a Majorana spinor.
          %p
            Then we use the following conventions on spacetime signature and the correspondig
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
          #MinkowskiSpacetime.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              We write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{s,t}
              for the real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo +
                        %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{s+t}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mi s
                    %mo +
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = s + t
              equipped with the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+form"} quadratic form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+of+a+quadratic+form"} signature
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (t,s)
              (“time”, “space”), i.e.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo +
                        %mi t
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    q(\vec x)
                    \\coloneqq
                    (x^1)^2
                    +
                    \\cdots
                    +
                    (x^s)^2
                    \-
                    (x^{s+1})^2
                    \-
                    \\cdots
                    \-
                    (x^{s+t})^2
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric"} metric
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi diag
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi t
                    %mo ,
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta = (\eta_{a b}) \coloneqq diag(\underset{t}{\underbrace{+1 , \cdots, +1}}, \underset{s}{\underbrace{-1, \cdots, -1}})
                    \\,.
            %p
              The real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(s,t)
              associated with this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
              is the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
              from elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo +
                        %mi t
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\Gamma_a\}_{0 = 1}^{s+t-1}
              subject to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo +
                    %mi s
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_a \Gamma_b + \Gamma_b \Gamma_a = 2 \eta_{a b}
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\forall a,b \in \{0,1,\cdots, t+s-1\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              For
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuples"} tuples
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_i)_{i = 1}^n
              of indices we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo !
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mn 1
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{a_1 \cdots a_n}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\Gamma_{[a_1}
                    \\cdots
                    \\Gamma_{a_2]}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\frac{1}{n!} \underset{\sigma}{\sum}
                    (-1)^{\vert \sigma\vert}
                    \\Gamma_{a_{\sigma_1}}
                    \\cdots
                    \\Gamma_{a_{\sigma_n}}
            %p
              for the skew-symmetrized product of Clifford generators with these indices. In partcular if all the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i
              are pairwise distinct, then this is simply the plain product of generators
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext if
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≠
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{a_1 \cdots a_n}
                    \=
                    \\Gamma_{a_1} \cdots \Gamma_{a_n}
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\text{if}
                    \\;
                    \\underset{i,j}{\forall} (a_i \neq a_j)
                    \\,.
          %p
            Indices are raised with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^{-1} = (\eta^{a b})
            (which of course as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            coincides with
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\eta_{a b})
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi a
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Gamma^a \coloneqq \eta^{a b} \Gamma_b
          #LorentzianSignature.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 1
              is that of
              = succeed "." do
                %strong Lorentzian signature
            %p
              In this case the single
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/timelike"} timelike
              Clifford genrator is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_0
              and the remaining spatial Clifford generators are
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_1, \Gamma_2, \cdots, \Gamma_{d-1}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma^0 = \Gamma_0
                  and
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Γ
                            %mn 0
                            %mn 2
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_0^2 = + 1
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi a
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma^a = - \Gamma_a
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_a^2 = -1
                  for
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \{1,\cdots, d-1\}
          %h3#DiracAndWeylRepresentations Dirac and Weyl representations
          %p
            The following is a standard convention for the complex representation of the Clifford algebra for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{s,1}
            (
            %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre"}> Castellani-D’Auria-Fré, (II.7.1)
            ):
          #CliffordAlgebraRepresentation.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              (
              %strong> Dirac representation
              )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 1
              (Lorentzian signature, def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LorentzianSignature"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mi s
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ν
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext for
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 4
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d = s + 1 \in \{ 2\nu, 2 \nu + 1 \}
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\text{for}\, \nu \in \mathbb{N}\,,\; d\geq 4
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then there is a choice of complex linear representation of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(s,1)
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MinkowskiSpacetime"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex vector space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V \coloneqq \mathbb{C}^{2^\nu}
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_{0}
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian"} hermitian
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi spatial
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_{spatial}
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-hermitian"} anti-hermitian
            %p Moreover, the pairing
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo †
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %mo ×
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\langle -,-\rangle \coloneqq (-)^\dagger \Gamma_0 (-)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    V \times V
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{C}
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+form"} hermitian form
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HermitianForms"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\omega^{a b} \Gamma_{a b})
              is
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation"} unitary
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo †
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_0^{-1} \exp(\omega^{a b} \Gamma_{a b})^{\dagger} \Gamma_0
                    \=
                    \\exp(\omega^{a b} \Gamma_{a b})^{-1}
                    \\,.
            %p
              These representations are called the
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+representations"} Dirac representations
              = succeed "." do
                %strong Dirac spinors
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              In the case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4
              consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pauli+matrices"} Pauli matrices
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi a
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\sigma_{a}\}_{a = 0}^3
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi a
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo +
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 2
                              %mo +
                              %mi i
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 3
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 2
                              %mo −
                              %mi i
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 3
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma_a x^a
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    x^0 + x^1 &amp; x^2 + i x^3
                    \\\
                    x^2 - i x^3 &amp; x^0 - x^1
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p Then a Clifford representation as claimed is given by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mi id
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi id
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_0
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; id
                    \\\
                    id &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi σ
                                %mi a
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msub
                                %mi σ
                                %mi a
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_a
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; \sigma_a
                    \\\
                    \-\sigma_a &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              From
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4
              we proceed to higher dimension by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            %p
              %strong odd dimensions
            %p
              Suppose a Clifford representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\gamma_a\}
              as claimed has been constructed in even dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                      %mi ν
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 2 \nu
            %p
              Then a Clifford representation in dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ν
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 2 \nu + 1
              is given by taking
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mi a
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi a
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi d
                              %mo −
                              %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ϵ
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mn 0
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mn 1
                              %mi ⋯
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi d
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi a
                              %mo =
                              %mi d
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_a
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\gamma_a &amp; \vert \; a \leq d - 2
                    \\\
                    \\epsilon \gamma_0 \gamma_1 \cdots \gamma_{d-2}
                    \&amp; \vert\; a = d-1
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p where
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi ν
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext odd
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi i
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi ν
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext even
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    1 &amp; \vert \; \nu \, \text{odd}
                    \\\
                    i &amp; \vert \; \nu \, \text{even}
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,.
            %p
              %strong even dimensions
            %p
              Suppose a Clifford representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\gamma_a\}
              as claimed has been constructed in even dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                      %mi ν
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 2 \nu
            %p
              Then a corresponding representation in dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+2
              is given by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi d
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mi a
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mi a
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mi id
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi id
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi i
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi i
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{a \lt d}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; \gamma_a
                    \\\
                    \\gamma_a &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\;\;\,,
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\Gamma_{d}
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; id
                    \\\
                    \-id &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\;\;\,,
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\Gamma_{d+1}
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    i \mathrm{id} &amp; 0
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; -i \mathrm{id}
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Finally regarding the statement that this gives a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation"} unitary representation
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo †
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle \coloneqq (-)^\dagger \Gamma_0 (-)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+form"} hermitian form
              follows since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_0
              obtained by the above construction is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+matrix"} hermitian matrix
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in \{1, \cdots, d-1\}
              be spacelike and distinct indices. Then by the above we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi b
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo †
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi b
                              %mo †
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                              %mo †
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi b
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\Gamma_0^{-1} (\Gamma_a \Gamma_b)^\dagger \Gamma_0
                    \&amp; =
                    \\Gamma_0^{-1} \Gamma_0 (\Gamma_b^\dagger \Gamma_a^\dagger)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = (-\Gamma_b) (-\Gamma_a)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = \Gamma_b \Gamma_a
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = - \Gamma_a \Gamma_b
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo †
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                              %mo †
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                              %mo †
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mn 0
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\Gamma_0^{-1} (\Gamma_0 \Gamma_a)^\dagger
                    \&amp; =
                    \- \Gamma_0^{-1} \Gamma_0 \Gamma_a^\dagger \Gamma_0^\dagger
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \- (- \Gamma_a) (\Gamma_0)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = \Gamma_a \Gamma_0
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = - \Gamma_0 \Gamma_a
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that the exponent of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\omega^{a b} \Gamma_a \Gamma_b)
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-hermitian+matrix"} anti-hermitian matrix
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary operator
          #WeylRepresentation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              (
              %strong> Weyl representation
              )
            %p
              Since by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CliffordAlgebraRepresentation"}
              the Dirac representations in dimensions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 2\nu
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ν
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+1 = 2\nu+1
              have the same underlying complex vector space, the element
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi d
                    %mo ∝
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{d}
                    \\propto
                    \\Gamma_0 \Gamma_1 \cdots \Gamma_{d-1}
            %p
              acts
              = succeed "-invariantly" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
              = succeed "-representation" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %p
              Moreover, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_0 \Gamma_1 \cdots \Gamma_{d-1}
              squares to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ±
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi c
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{d+1} \coloneqq c \Gamma_0 \Gamma_1 \cdots \Gamma_{d-1}
            %p
              squares to +1. This is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %strong chirality operator
            %p
              (The notation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_{d+1}
              for this operator originates from times when only
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4
              was considered. Clearly this notation has its pitfalls when various
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              are considered, but nevertheless it is commonly used this way e.g.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} Castellani-D’Auria-Fré, section (II.7.11) and top of p. 523
            %p
              Therefore this representation decomposes as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo +
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V = V_+ \oplus V_-
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenspaces"} eigenspaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{\pm}
              of the chirality operator, respectively. These
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{\pm}
              are called the two
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+representations"} Weyl representations
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
              %strong chiral spinor
              (“left handed”, “right handed”, respectively).
          #DiracConjugate.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              For a Clifford algebra representation on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^\nu
              as in prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CliffordAlgebraRepresentation"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
