              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \mathbb{C}^\nu
              as above. Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\Gamma_a\}
              for a Dirac representation according to prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CliffordAlgebraRepresentation"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mtext for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi d
                              %mo =
                              %mn 4
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mtext for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi d
                              %mo =
                              %mn 8
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mtext for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi d
                              %mo =
                              %mn 9
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi or
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mtext for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi d
                              %mo =
                              %mn 10
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mtext for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi d
                              %mo =
                              %mn 11
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    C_{(-)} &amp; \text{for}\; d = 4
                    \\\
                    C_{(+)} &amp; \text{for}\; d = 8
                    \\\
                    C_{(+)} &amp; \text{for}\; d = 9
                    \\\
                    C_{(+)} or C_{(-)} &amp; \text{for}\; d = 10
                    \\\
                    C_{(-)} &amp; \text{for}\; d = 11
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
              for the choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+conjugation+matrix"} charge conjugation matrix
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ChargeConjugationMatrix"}
              as shown. Then the function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J \colon V \longrightarrow V
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi C
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                      %mi T
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
