                    \\,.
          %h2#Supersymmetry Supersymmetry: Super-Poincaré and super-Minkowski
          %p
            Every real spin representation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} extension
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1})
            in that dimension, i.e. of the Lie algebra of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MinkowskiSpacetime"}
          %p
            Since we may recover a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            from its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
            as the (vector space underlying the)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
            by the Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(d-1,1)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+Lie+algebra"} orthogonal Lie algebra
            in Lorentian signature)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi 𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1})/\mathfrak{so}(d-1,1)
          %p
            (namely as the Lie algebra of translations along itself), every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+Lie+algebras"} extension
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
            defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+Lie+algebras"} extension
            of Minkowski spacetime. These extensions are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert N}
            of the following definition, and this justifies the following notation:
          #SuperMinkowskiSpacetime.num_defn
            %h6#definition_12 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathbb{N}
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in Rep(Spin(d-1,1))
              be a real spin representation, hence a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of Majorana representations (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MajoranaRepresentation"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeylMajorana"}
            %p
              We define the corresponding
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
            %p
              equivalently in terms of its
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N}))
              (a
              = succeed "-bigraded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
            %p This is generated on
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e^a\}
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\omega^{ a b}\}
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,even)
              %li
                %p
                  and elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\psi^\alpha\}
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,odd)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \{0,1, \cdots, d-1\}
              is a spacetime index, and where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              is an index ranging over a basis of the chosen Majorana spinor representation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %p The CE-differential is defined as follows
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, \omega^{a b} = \omega^a{}_b \wedge \omega^{b c}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 4
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mi ψ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, \psi = \frac{1}{4} \omega^{ a b} \Gamma_{a b} \psi
                    \\,.
            %p
              (which so far is the differential for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"} semidirect product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acting
              on the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
              representation)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, e^{a } = \omega^a{}_b \wedge e^b + \overline{\psi} \Gamma^a \psi
            %p
              where on the right we have the spinor-to-vector pairing in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpinorToVectorBilinearPairing"}
            %p
              That this is indeed a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              follows from the fact that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              and the fact that the spinor-to-vector pairing is symmetric (which makes it qualify as the odd-odd component of a super-Lie algebra) and
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
              for it), all according to prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpinorToVectorPairing"}
            %p
              This defines the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+super+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré super Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              this becomes the CE algebra of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+algebra"} super translation algebra
              underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert N}
                    \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#InDimensions11And10And9 In dimensions 11, 10, and 9
          %p
            We spell out some of the above constructions and properties for Majorana spinors in Lorentzian spacetimes (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LorentzianSignature"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            in 10d and 9d, as well as to the relation between these via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactification"} Kaluza-Klein compactification
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
          #DiracRepInD11FromD9.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_12 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\gamma_a\}
              be any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+representation"} Dirac representation
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8,1)
              according to prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CliffordAlgebraRepresentation"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CliffordAlgebraRepresentation"}
              we get from this the Dirac representations in dimensions 9+1 and 10+1 by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 8
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mi a
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mi a
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 9
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mi id
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi id
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 10
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi i
                              %mi id
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi i
                              %mi id
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{a \leq 8}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; \gamma_a
                    \\\
                    \\gamma_a &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\;\,,\;\;
                    \\Gamma_{9}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; id
                    \\\
                    \-id &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\;\,,\;\;
                    \\Gamma_{10}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    i id &amp; 0
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; -i id
