                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          #SpinRepsFrom11dToTDuality.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CliffordAlgebraRepresentation"}
              the Dirac representation in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 11
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 11
              has complex dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mn 10
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mn 5
                      %mo =
                      %mn 32
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{10/2} = 2^{5} = 32
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MajoranaConjugationIsRealStructure"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheMajoranaConditionInComponents"}
              this representation carries a real structure and hence gives a real/Majorana
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}^{32}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(10,1)
              of real dimension 32. This representation often just called “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
              ”. This way the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
              (remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperPoincareOutlook"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 10
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
            %p
              which thus serves to express both, the real dimension of the space of odd-graded coordinate functions at every point on it, as well as the way that the
              = succeed "-cover" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(10,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(10,1)
              acts on these. This is the local model space for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetimes"} super spacetimes
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %p
              As we regard
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^{32}
              instead as the Dirac representation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 9
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(9,1)
              via def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeylRepresentation"}
            %p
              Since in 10d the Weyl condition is compatible with the Majorana condition (by prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeylMajoranaInLorentzian10d"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
              correspondingly decomposes as a direct sum two real representations of dimension 116 which often are denoted
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 16
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{16}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 16
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbf{16}}
              = succeed "-representations" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 9
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(9,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              decomposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                    %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 16
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                      %mo ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{32} \simeq \mathbf{16} \oplus \overline{\mathbf{16}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
              (remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperPoincareOutlook"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 9
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 16
                        %mo +
                        %mover
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 16
                          %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{9,1\vert \mathbf{16} + \overline{\mathbf{16}}}
            %p
              is said to be of “type IIA”, since this is the local model space for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetimes"} superspacetimes
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+supergravity"} type IIA supergravity
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 9
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 16
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 16
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{9,1\vert \mathbf{16}\oplus \mathbf{16}}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 9
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 16
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{9,1\vert \mathbf{16}}
              which is “heterotic” (the local model space for
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            %p
              Now the Dirac-Weyl representation for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8,1)
              is of complex dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mn 8
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mn 4
                      %mo =
                      %mn 16
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 2^{8/2} = 2^4 = 16
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MajoranaConjugationIsRealStructure"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheMajoranaConditionInComponents"}
              this also admits real structure, and hence gives a Majorana representation fro
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 8
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{16}
            %p
              We want to argue that both the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 16
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{16}
              and the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbf{16}}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 9
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(9,1)
              become isomorphic to the single
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 16
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{16}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8,1)
              under forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+representation"} restricted representation
              along the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 9
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8,1)\hookrightarrow Spin(9,1)
              (the one fixed by the above choice of components).
            %p
              For this it is sufficient to see that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 9
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_9
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 9
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 16
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_9 \colon \mathbf{16} \longrightarrow \overline{\mathbf{16}}
              constitutes an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              when regarded as a morphism in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of representations
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 8
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8,1)
            %p
              Clearly it is a linear isomorphism, so it is sufficient that it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              = succeed "-representations" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 8
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 9
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_9
              commutes with all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_a \Gamma_b
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} on
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 8
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \on \{0,\cdots, 8\}
            %p
              Hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branching+rule"} branching rule
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+representation"} restricting
              the Weyl representation in 11d along the sequence of inclusions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 9
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 10
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Spin(8,1) \hookrightarrow Spin(9,1) \hookrightarrow Spin(10,1)
            %p is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 32
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Rep
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 10
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 16
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mover
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 16
                            %mo ¯
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Rep
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 9
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 16
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 16
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Rep
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 8
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{\in Rep(Spin(10,1))}\underbrace{\mathbf{32}}
                    \\mapsto
                    \\underset{\in Rep(Spin(9,1))}\underbrace{\mathbf{16} \oplus \overline{\mathbf{16}}}
                    \\mapsto
                    \\underset{\in Rep(Spin(8,1))}\underbrace{\mathbf{16} \oplus \mathbf{16}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              If we write a Majorana spinor in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
              as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϑ
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mn 32
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vartheta \in \mathbb{C}^{32}
              = succeed "-matrix" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %mn 32
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 \times 32)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϑ
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi ψ
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi ψ
                                %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\vartheta
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \\psi_1
                    \\\
                    \\psi_2
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p and if we write for short
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi ψ
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi ψ
                                %mn 2
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\psi_1
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \\psi_1 \\ 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,,\;\;\;
                    \\psi_2
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 \\  \psi_2
                    }
                    \\right)
            %p
              then this says that after restriction to
              = succeed "-action" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 9
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(9,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_1
              becomes a Majorana spinor in the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{16}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_2
              a Majorana spinor in the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 16
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbf{16}}
              = succeed "-action" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 8
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{16}
          %p The type IIA spinor-to-vector pairing is just that of 11d under this re-interpretation. We find:
          #typeIIASpinorToVectorPairing.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_13 Proposition
            %p The type IIA spinor-to-vector pairing is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mrow
                                  %mtable
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ψ
                                          %mn 1
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ψ
                                          %mn 2
                                %mo )
                              %mo ¯
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                              %mi IIA
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ψ
                                        %mn 1
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ψ
                                        %mn 2
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
