            %h6#proof_14 Proof
            %p
              To see that the given 2-forms are indeed cocycles: they are trivially closed (by def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^\alpha
              are in bidegree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi odd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,odd)
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpinorToVectorPairing"}
            %p
              Now to see the extensions. Notice that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              any (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"}> super
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              (of finite dimension, for convenience), and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \wedge^2\mathfrak{g}^\ast
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra 2-cocycle
              on it, then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} Lie algebra extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\mathfrak{g}}
              that this classifies is neatly characterized in terms of its dual
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
