          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (application in 11d supergravity)
              %br/
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
              the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form+on+a+supermanifold"} super 1-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi dR
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ;
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \in \Omega^1_{dR}(-;\mathbf{32}_1)
              of de Rham degree 1 with coefficients in a copy of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
              in odd degree. By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} super-sign rule
              this means that these forms actuall commute with each other, hence that the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(10,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+function"} equivariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combinations"} linear combinations
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+products"} wedge products
              of these gravitino fields are
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(10,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
              seen on the left of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:IrrepDecompositionOfSymmetricPowersOf32"} (2)
            %p
              Now
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur%27s+lemma"} Schur's lemma
              implies that such cobinations can be non-zero only if they take values in the irreps appearing on the right of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:IrrepDecompositionOfSymmetricPowersOf32"} (2)
            %p
              For example, the only
              = succeed "-equiariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(10,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi sym
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{32} \otimes \mathbf{32})_{sym} \to \mathbf{32}
              must be zero, which implies for instance that the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi dR
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ;
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 32
                        %mi odd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \in \Omega^2_{dR}(-;\mathbf{32}_{odd})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi a
                    %mi ψ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mover
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ¯
                          %mi κ
                          %mi ψ
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho
                    \\;=\;
                    \\rho_{a b}
                    e^a\, e^b
                    +
                    H_a \psi \, e^a
                    +
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\overline{\psi}\kappa\psi
                    }_{ =  0}
                    \\,,
            %p
              has to have vanishing last component
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              has to be pointwise just such a
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(10,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
