          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fierz+identities"} Fierz identities
                controlling
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
              %br/
              The following quartic expressions in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} pin
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pin \in \mathbf{32}
              vanish:
            #eq:QuarticFierzIdentitiesOn32.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ¯
                          %msub
                            %mi Γ
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                              %mi b
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ¯
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msup
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi a
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ¯
                          %msub
                            %mi Γ
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                              %msub
                                %mi b
                                %mn 1
                              %mi ⋯
                              %msub
                                %mi b
                                %mn 4
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ¯
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msup
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi a
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo +
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mn 3
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ¯
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi Γ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi b
                                %mn 1
                              %msub
                                %mi b
                                %mn 2
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ¯
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi Γ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi b
                                %mn 3
                              %msub
                                %mi b
                                %mn 4
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{r}
                    \\big(
                    \\overline{\psi}
                    \\Gamma_{a b}
                    \\psi
                    \\big)
                    \\big(
                    \\overline{\psi}
                    \\,\Gamma^{a}\,
                    \\psi
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    0
                    \\\
                    \\big(
                    \\overline{\psi}
                    \\Gamma_{a b_1\cdots b_4}
                    \\psi
                    \\big)
                    \\big(
                    \\overline{\psi}
                    \\,\Gamma^{a}\,
                    \\psi
                    \\big)
                    \\;+\;
                    3
                    \\,
                    \\big(
                    \\overline{\psi}
                    \\,\Gamma_{b_1 b_2}\,
                    \\psi
                    \\big)
                    \\big(
                    \\overline{\psi}
                    \\,\Gamma_{b_3 b_4}\,
                    \\psi
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    0
                    \\end{array}
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              On the first expression: This is the quartic diagonal of a
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 10
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spin}(1,10)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 32
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} symm
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 11
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    \\mathbf{32}
                    \\,\otimes\,
                    \\mathbf{32}
                    \\,\otimes\,
                    \\mathbf{32}
                    \\,\otimes\,
                    \\mathbf{32}
                    \\big)_{\mathrm{symm}}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbf{11}
                    \\,.
            %p
              But by
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:IrrepDecompositionOfSymmetricPowersOf32"} (2)
              the irrep summand
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 11
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{11}
              does not appear on the left, hence this map has to vanish by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur%27s+lemma"} Schur's lemma
              (
              %a{:href => "D'Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity#DAuriaFre82"}> D’Auria &amp; Fré 1982, (3.13)
              ). For the second expression one needs a closer analysis (
              %a{:href => "D'Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity#DAuriaFre82"}> D’Auria &amp; Fré 1982, (3.28a)
              ; also
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#NaitoOsadaKukui86"} Naito, Osada &amp; Kukui 1986, (2.27) and (2.28)
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes#TheM2andM5CocyclesAsFierzIdentities"} this example
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} geometry of physics – fundamental super p-branes
          %h2#appendix Appendix
          %h3#review_of_unitary_representations_with_real_structure Review of unitary representations with real structure
          %p
            For reference, we here collect some basics regarding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representations"} unitary representations
            equipped with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real structure
          %p
            All
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            in the following are taken to be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite dimensional vector spaces
          #RealStructure.num_defn
            %h6#definition_14 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex vector space
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real structure
              or
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+structure"} quaternionic structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is a real-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi \;\colon\; V \longrightarrow V
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                  is conjugate linear (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi λ
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mover
                          %mi λ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(\lambda v) = \overline{\lambda} \phi(v)
                  for all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi λ
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℂ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in \mathbb{C}
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                  %mi id
                                %mtd
                                  %mtext for real structure
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi id
                                %mtd
                                  %mtext for quaternionic structure
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^2 = \left\{ \array{ +id &amp; \text{for real structure} \\ -id &amp; \text{for quaternionic structure} }  \right.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              A real structure
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealStructure"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              corresponds to a choice of complex linear isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V \simeq \mathbb{C} \otimes_{\mathbb{R}} V_+
            %p
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complexification"} complexification
              of a real vector space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_+
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenspace"} eigenspace
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalue"} eigenvalue
              +1, while
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo −
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_- \coloneqq i V_+
              is the eigenspace of eigenvalue -1.
            %p
              A quaternionic structure, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealStructure"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              gives it the structure of a left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
              extending the underlying structure of a module over the complex numbers. Namely let
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \coloneqq i(-) \colon V \to V
                  be the operation of acting with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℂ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathbb{C}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \coloneqq \phi \colon V \to V
                  be the given endomorphisms,
            %p
              then the conjugate complex linearity of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              means that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J \circ I = - I \circ J
            %p
              and hence with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^2 = -1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^2 = -1
              this means that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \coloneqq I \circ J
              act like the imaginary quaternions.
          #RealStructureOnLinearRepresentation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_15 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex vector space
              and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho \;\colon\; G \longrightarrow GL_{\mathbb{C}}(V)
            %p
              be a complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representation"} linear representation
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
              form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            %p
              Then a
              %em real structure
              or
              %em quaternionic structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\rho)
              is a real or complex structure, respectively,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealStructure"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is
              = succeed "-invariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi \circ \rho(g) = \rho(g) \circ \phi
                    \\,.
          %p
            We will be interested in complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite dimensional vector spaces
            equipped with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+forms"} hermitian forms
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
          #HermitianForms.num_defn
            %h6#definition_16 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+form"} hermitian form
              (or symmetric complex
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sesquilinear+form"} sesquilinear form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is a real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %mo ×
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\langle
                    \-,-
                    \\rangle
                    \\;\colon\;
                    V \times V
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{C}
            %p
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1, v_2 \in V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in \mathbb{C}
              then
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (sesquilinearity)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi λ
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo =
                          %mi λ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle v_1, \lambda v_2 \rangle = \lambda \langle v_1, v_2 \rangle
              %li
                %p
                  (conjugate symmetry)
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 2
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                            %mo *
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle v_1, v_2\rangle^\ast = \langle v_2, v_1\rangle
              %li
                %p
                  (non-degeneracy) if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle v_1,-\rangle = 0
                  then
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1 = 0
            %p
              A complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon V \to V
              is
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary
              with respect to this hermitian form if it preserves it, in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\langle f(-), f(-)\rangle
                    \=
                    \\langle -,-\rangle
                    \\,.
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U(V) \hookrightarrow GL_{\mathbb{C}}(V)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operators"} unitary operators
              inside the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %p
              A complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representation"} linear representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \colon G \longrightarrow GL_{\mathbb{C}}(V)
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation"} unitary representation
              if it factors through this subgroup
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho \;\colon\;  G \longrightarrow U(V) \hookrightarrow GL_{\mathbb{C}}(V)
                    \\,.
          %p The following proposition uses assumptions stronger than what we have in the application to Majorana spinors (compact Lie group, positive definite hermitian form) but it nevertheless helps to see the pattern.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_18 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle
              some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+definite+bilinear+form"} positive definite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+form"} hermitian form
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HermitianForms"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \colon G \to U(V)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation"} unitary representation
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              carries a real structure or quaternionc structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealStructureOnLinearRepresentation"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+map"} bilinear map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-,-) \;\colon\; V \otimes_{\mathbb{C}} V \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}
                    \\,.
            %p Explicitly:
            %p
              Given a real/quaternionic structure
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-,-) \coloneqq \langle \phi(-), -\rangle
                    \\,.
            %p
              Conversely, given
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-,-)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \phi
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mover
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-,-) = \langle \tilde\phi(-),-\rangle
                    \\,,
            %p
              and then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ≔
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \coloneqq \frac{1}{\vert \phi\vert} \phi
              is the corresponding real/quaternionic structure.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo =
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde\phi = \phi
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-,-)
              is called
              %em compatible
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle-,- \rangle
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Meinrenken13"} Meinrenken 13, p. 81
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+conjugation+matrix"} charge conjugation matrix
            %li
              %p
                only vaguely related:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+zero+modes"} Majorana zero modes
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Named after
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ettore+Majorana"} Ettore Majorana
          %p
            The traditional component discussion in terms of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+conjugation+matrix"} charge conjugation matrix
            is discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#CastellaniDAuriaFre
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supergravity+and+Superstrings+-+A+Geometric+Perspective"} Supergravity and Superstrings - A Geometric Perspective
            %li#VanProeyen99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antoine+Van+Proeyen"}> Antoine Van Proeyen
                , section 3 of
                %em Tools for supersymmetry
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9910030"}> arXiv:hep-th/9910030
                )
            %li#Laenen
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Laenen"}> Eric Laenen
                ,
                %em Classical Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.nikhef.nl/~t45/ftip/"}> web
                ) chapter on
                %em Gamma matrices
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.nikhef.nl/~t45/ftip/AppendixE.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p The relation to the concept of real structures on complex Spin-representations is highlighted in
          %ul
